# Box-wide tool credentials, sourced by every shell (~/.bashrc.d/devbox.sh).
# Bootstrap installs this template as ~/.config/devbox/secrets.env at mode 600
# and never fills it; it lives on the bind mount, so it survives every rebuild.
#
# Plain KEY=value pairs only - no `export`, no `op://` references. The container
# holds no 1Password account by design (docs/secrets.md): render values on the
# laptop, where approving access is yours to do, and copy them in.
#
# What belongs here: credentials every project shares, i.e. the tools' own.
# What does not: anything a single project needs. Project secrets go in that
# project's .env so a leak stays scoped to one project - GCP included, since
# each project has its own GCP project and therefore its own ADC key path.

# GitHub CLI, one token per identity: GH_TOKEN_<SLUG>, upper-cased from the
# `[slug]` in ~/.config/devbox/identities.conf. The working directory picks
# which one is used, on the same rule git uses for identities - the `dir`
# prefixes in that file, longest match first, with the one identity that has no
# `dir` catching everything else (`devbox-gh-token --account` reports which).
#
# Keep each one fine-grained and expiring. Where no GitHub App is installed,
# this PAT is what agents act with - git push through `devbox-git-credential`
# and every `gh` command - so it needs contents, pull-requests, issues and
# actions write, commit statuses read. Where the App is installed,
# agents use the App instead and this PAT needs only metadata read plus what you
# run by hand. Tables: docs/secrets.md, "Permissions per token". Your own
# `git push` never uses these - that goes over SSH through the forwarded
# 1Password agent.
#
# Unlike the rest of this file, these are never exported: `devbox-gh-token`
# reads them from here by name on every call, so no other process holds them
# and a new token works without reconnecting.
#
# Do NOT define a plain GH_TOKEN here: it overrides every per-identity variable
# and disables the per-directory choice for every tree. For a one-off, pass it
# per command instead: GH_TOKEN=<other> gh ...
# GH_TOKEN_PERSONAL=github_pat_...
# GH_TOKEN_WORK=github_pat_...

# Optional model API keys, only for a provider OMP should use by key - OMP
# logs in with a subscription through /login and needs none of these. Claude
# Code never sees ANTHROPIC_API_KEY: claude-launcher unsets it, so Claude runs
# on its /login subscription instead of billing this key.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
